##########################################################
## Implicit dynamic analysis of a quasi-static load.
## The load is ramped over the first half of the analysis and held constant over
## the second half, with a density light enough that inertia is negligible, so
## the final state must agree with the static solution of the same problem
## (peak U3 = -7.640e-01, monitored node 3121 U3 = -7.613e-01).
## The constant-load half starts each step already in equilibrium. A convergence
## check normalized by the initial residual of the substep therefore demands an
## arbitrarily small absolute residual there and runs out of iterations; one
## normalized by the internal force converges in the minimum number of
## iterations. See issue #96.
##########################################################
!VERSION
 3
!SOLUTION, TYPE=DYNAMIC, NONLINEAR
!DYNAMIC, TYPE=NONLINEAR
 1 , 1
 0.0, 100.0, 10, 10.0
 0.5, 0.25
 1, 1, 0.0, 0.0
 100, 3121, 1
 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0
###################################
#####   BOUNDARY CONDITIONS   #####
###################################
!BOUNDARY, GRPID=1
  FIX, 1, 3, 0.0
!CLOAD, GRPID=1, AMP=AMP1
  CL1, 3, -1.0
###################################
#####         MATERIAL        #####
###################################
!MATERIAL, NAME=M1
!ELASTIC
  4000.0, 0.3
!DENSITY
  1.0e-06
###################################
#####       SOLVER CONTROL    #####
###################################
!SOLVER,METHOD=CG,PRECOND=3,ITERLOG=NO,TIMELOG=NO
  10000, 1, 10, 10
 1.0e-08, 1.0, 0.0
###################################
#####       STEP CONTROL      #####
###################################
!STEP, SUBSTEPS=10, MAXITER=20, CONVERG=1.0e-6
 10.0, 100.0
 BOUNDARY, 1
 LOAD, 1
!WRITE,RESULT,FREQUENCY=9999
!OUTPUT_RES
 DISP,ON
!END
